@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Homepage paint monitoring
+
+`performance-monitor.js` observes contentful paints from the navigation links,
+Order Now, and Seasonal Favorites cards. Stable `data-performance-action` values
+identify the initiating control, including clicks on nested content and keyboard
+activation. It does not intercept clicks or change link destinations.
+
+Read the latest 100 reports with `window.dailyGrindPerformance.getReports()`.
+Subscribe to `window`'s `daily-grind:performance` event to connect your analytics
+transport; the report is in `event.detail`. No data is sent over the network.
+`window.dailyGrindPerformance.support` exposes feature availability.
+
+- `interaction-contentful-paint`: `action`, `interactionId`, `startTime`,
+  `duration` in milliseconds from input to presentation, and painted `size`.
+  Successive reports are progressively larger contentful paint candidates for
+  that interaction, including content rendered after asynchronous work.
+- `soft-navigation`: destination `path`, initiating action (when available),
+  interaction/navigation IDs, `startTime`, `fcpDuration`, `lcpDuration`, `lcpSize`,
+  and `final`. The first report seeds LCP from content already painted before
+  the URL changed. The final report incorporates subsequent paints from the
+  same interaction and is emitted on the next soft navigation or page hide.
+
+These APIs are a progressive enhancement: unsupported browsers skip the
+corresponding observers. Missing data is not reported as a zero duration.
+Contentful paint candidates measure when relevant text/images appear, rather
+than guaranteeing all animations or application work have finished. They are
+not INP or initial-load LCP.
+
+The current homepage has ordinary full-document links and no client router.
+Soft-navigation reports appear only when a trusted interaction causes an actual
+client-side URL and content update. A full-document navigation's destination
+paint cannot be measured by the departing homepage script; the destination
+would need its own navigation timing instrumentation. URL-only changes and
+clicks that do not produce a contentful paint do not produce invented results.
+
+Run `node --test tests/performance-monitor.test.cjs` for isolated observer tests.
+No browser or server is needed.
